## Project structure

```
src/
├── components/
│   └── QuoteModal.tsx   # Lead form modal
├── context/
│   └── QuoteContext.tsx # openQuote / closeQuote
├── data/
│   └── menus.ts         # Demo menu configs + formatBRL / getMenuBySlug
├── lib/
│   └── email.ts         # FormSubmit quote submit
├── pages/
│   ├── LandingPage.tsx  # Marketing LP
│   └── MenuPage.tsx     # Demo cardápio + cart
├── types.ts             # QuoteFormData, MenuConfig, CartLine, …
├── index.css            # Tailwind v4 + @theme tokens
├── App.tsx              # BrowserRouter + routes
└── main.tsx

public/                  # favicon, icons
vite.config.ts
index.html
```

---

## Architecture conventions

- **Routing:** Routes live in `src/App.tsx` (`/` and `/cardapio/:slug`). Use `basename` from `import.meta.env.BASE_URL` when needed.
- **Imports:** Relative imports within `src/` (no `@/` alias today). Named exports for pages/components; `App` may stay default for Vite entry.
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`. Tokens in `src/index.css` `@theme` (`ink`, `lime`, `accent`, fonts Syne/Manrope). Prefer existing utility classes and theme colors.
- **Types:** Domain types in `src/types.ts`.
- **Menus:** Add/edit demos only in `src/data/menus.ts`; slug must match route param.
- **Quotes:** All CTAs call `openQuote(source)`; do not bypass `QuoteModal` / FormSubmit path without explicit product change.
- **No backend:** Do not introduce Supabase, serverless `api/`, or auth unless product scope expands and rules/skills are updated.

---

## Brand / UI notes

- Brand: **Cardápio Livre** — lime accent on dark ink greens; Outfit (display) + Manrope (body).
- Demo menus use per-client `theme` colors from `menus.ts`.
- Keep marketing copy in Portuguese (pt-BR).

---

## Efficiency

Scope prompts precisely (e.g. one page, one menu slug, quote form field). Less context loaded means fewer tokens and clearer answers.
